# 🌪️ .windsurf — Windsurf IDE Agent Rules

> **For:** Windsurf IDE + Antigravity Agent  
> **Status:** Active (2026-05-30)

---

## QUICK START

```bash
git pull origin main
cat .ai_context.md
cat strategy.md
cat .cursorrules  # (for full rules)
```

---

## CORE PRINCIPLES

| Principle | Meaning |
|-----------|---------|
| **Local-First** | SQLite primary, no cloud-first |
| **Decision-First** | High-depth analytics, not raw data |
| **CLI-First** | Scripts need `--help` |
| **Text-First** | JSON + Markdown output |
| **Caveat Layer** | Quality flags on every metric |

---

## WHAT YOU CAN DO

✅ Write CLI scripts  
✅ SQL optimization  
✅ Mathematical calculations  
✅ Tests + documentation  
✅ Update Knowledge Base

## WHAT YOU CANNOT DO

❌ Modify `strategy.md`  
❌ Change database schema  
❌ Add dependencies  
❌ Make UI/UX changes  
❌ Change architecture

---

## KNOWLEDGE BASE

Before coding: `cat knowledge_base/decisions/FEATURE_PRIORITIES.md`  
For patterns: `cat knowledge_base/docs/BEST_PRACTICES.md`  
For errors: `cat knowledge_base/learnings/COMMON_ERRORS_AND_WORKAROUNDS.md`

---

## CURRENT TASK

Build Anomaly Detector CLI (see `scripts/analytics/README.md`)

---

## WORKFLOW

```
git pull → read .ai_context.md → read strategy.md → code → test → commit → (if limits: update .ai_context.md + commit)
```

---

## WHEN UNSURE

Use DECISION FORMAT (A1/A2/A3 options, not open-ended)

---

## CRITICAL RULES

1. Read `.ai_context.md` every session start
2. Never modify `strategy.md` directly
3. Always inject caveats
4. Always output JSON + Markdown
5. Always test before commit
6. Always ask if unsure

---

For detailed rules: `cat .cursorrules`  
For onboarding: `cat handshake.md`
